		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3671&amp;p=28601#p28601"><![CDATA[
Please will anyone who has the UV380/390 PLUS version, whether it works correctly or not with the OpenGD77 firmware,  use the "Backup registers" function in the CPS, and zip the file and then post it here<br><br>In the CPS. <br>Make sure you select the Radio Type as MD-9600/UV380 etc<br>In the Extras menu item select "OpenGD77 support"<br>On the OpenGD77 support screen, press the "Backup registers" button.<br><br>This will prompt to save the file.<br><br>After the file has been saved, zip it and post it here<br><br>We need this data for multiple versions of the UV380/390 PLUS  radios, both 5W and 10W to try to understand the manufacturer settuings which may be affecting the display operation on the 10W version of the UV380/390<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Thu Jan 11, 2024 6:49 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
